{"id":"word:hebrew:H4150","type":"word","title":"מוֹעֵד","subtitle":"H4150 • Hebrew word","simple":{"meaning":"properly, an appointment , i.e. a fixed time or season; specifically, a festival ; conventionally a year ; by implication, an assembly (as convened for a definite purpose); technically the congregation ; by extension, the place of meeting ; also a signal (as appointed beforehand)","inThisVerse":"The selected word is tied to מוֹעֵד (H4150) in the Hebrew source text. Part of speech: n-m.","whyItMatters":"This word appears 223 times in the Hebrew Bible, so BibleIQ can compare how Scripture uses it across multiple passages.","summary":"מוֹעֵד (môwʻêd) means properly, an appointment , i.e. a fixed time or season; specifically, a festival ; conventionally a year ; by implication, an assembly (as convened for a definite purpose); technically the congregation ; by extension, the place of meeting ; also a signal (as appointed beforehand) First listed occurrence: 1Chr 6 17."},"evidence":{"originalLanguage":{"source":"hebrew","word":"מוֹעֵד","transliteration":"môwʻêd","pronunciation":"mo-ade'","strong":"H4150","lemmaId":"hebrew:H4150","partOfSpeech":"n-m","forms":["מוֹעֵֽד","מוֹעֵ֑ד","מוֹעֵ֔ד","מוֹעֵ֖ד","מוֹעֵד֙"],"morphs":[["HNcmsa",160],["HRd/Ncmsa",12],["HNcmpc",7],["HR/Ncmsc/Sp3ms",6],["HR/Ncmsc",5],["HC/Rd/Ncmpa",4],["HTd/Ncmsa",3],["HR/Ncmsa",3],["HNcmpc/Sp1cs",2],["HRd/Ncmpa",2]]},"definitions":{"short":"properly, an appointment , i.e. a fixed time or season; specifically, a festival ; conventionally a year ; by implication, an assembly (as convened for a definite purpose); technically the congregation ; by extension, the place of meeting ; also a signal (as appointed beforehand)","usage":"appointed (sign, time), (place of, solemn) assembly, congregation, (set, solemn) feast, (appointed, due) season, solemn(-ity), synogogue, (set) time (appointed).","full":"H4150. moed מוֺעֵד 223 noun masculine Psa 102:14 appointed time, place, meeting ; ׳מ Exod 9:5 183t.; מֹעֵד Deut 31:10 ; מוֺעֲדוֺ Num 9:2 2 t.; מֹעֲדוֺ Lam 2:6 3 t. + 5 t. suffixes; plural מוֺעֲדִים Dan 12:7 6 t.; מֹעֲדִים Zech 8:19 ; 1Chr 23:31 ; מוֺעֲדוֺת 2Chr 8:13 ; construct מֹועֲדֵי Lev 23:2 6 t.; מֹעֲדֵי 23:44 ; suffixes מוֺעֲדַי Ezek 44:24 ; מֹעֲדֵיכֶם Num 15:3 6 t. suffixes; — 1 appointed time: a. in General with prefix לְ , at an or the appointed time Gen 18:14 ; Exod 13:10 (J), 23:15 ; 34:18 ; Josh 8:14 (all J E), Gen 17:21 ; 21:2 (P), 1Sam 9:24 ; 13:8 (after אשׁר insert either ᵑ7 ᵐ5 אָמַר or שָׂם Dr), 13:11 ; 2Kin 4:16-17 , Hab 2:3 ; Dan 8:19 ; 11:27 , 29 , 35 ; ׳למ דוד at he time appointed with David 1Sam 20:35 (Thes SS place appointed ); with prefix בְּ Hosea 2:11 ; Lev 23:4 ; Num 9:2-3 , 7 , 13 ; 28:2 (P); with מִן 2Sam 20:5 ; עֵת מ׳עַד 24:15 unto the time appointed (but dubious, see Dr); with verbs מ ׳בא Psa 102:14 ; מ ׳לקח 75:3 ; מ ׳שׂים Exod 9:5 (J); המ ׳העביר Jer 46:17 ; the stork מ ׳ידעה 8:7 knows her appointed time ; ׳מ צאתך Deut 16:6 time of thy going forth (from Egypt). b. in particular (compare Exod 13:10 ; 23:15 ; 34:18 ), sacred season , RV usually set feast or appointed season (wider than חַג , which was only a feast celebrated by a pilgrimage ), מ (ימי) ׳יוֺם day ( s ) of appointed season (i.e. festivals ) Hosea 9:5 ; 12:10 ; Lam 2:7 , 22 ; singular indefinite 1:4 ; of the feast of booths Deut 31:10 ; || שׁבת חדשׁ חג Hosea 2:13 ; || שׁבת Lam 2:6 ; usually plural ׳מ יהוה Lev 23:2 , 4 , 37 , 44 (P), 2Chr 2:3 Ezra 3:5 ; with suffixes referring to ׳י Lev 23:2 (P); ׳בּמ Num 15:3 ; 29:39 (P), Ezek 36:38 ; 46:9 ; ׳מ קרית city of our solemnities (sacred seasons) Isa 33:20 ; ׳למ טובים Zech 8:19 ; || שׁבתות Ezek 44:24 ; || חדשׁים Isa 1:14 ; 1Chr 23:31 ; 2Chr 8:13 ; 31:3 ; Neh 10:34 ; || חנים Ezek 46:11 ; חדשׁים חגים 45:17 ; || חָדְשֵׁכֶם ראשׁי Num 10:10 (P). — Notes. It is most probable that in Gen 1:14 (P), where ׳מ || אֹתֹת , the reference is to the sacred seasons as fixed by moon's appearance; and so also למ ירח ׳עשׂה he made the moon for sacred seasons Psa 104:19 , although many Lexicons & Commentaries refer these to the seasons of the year. — וחצי מועדים למועד Dan 12:7 for a set time, times, and a half = 3 2-Janappointed times = half the prophetic week of years, compare Br MP 453 f. — המ את ׳ויאכלו they ate throughout the sacred season (of Maƒƒoth ) 2Chr 30:22 AV RV, but Thes SS Be Ke Öttli they ate the offerings of the sacred season ; וַיְכַלּוּ ᵐ5 . 2 appointed meeting: מ ׳בֵּית לְכָלחַֿי Job 30:23 house of meeting for every living (of She'ol); מ ׳קְרִאֵי Num 16:2 (P) called to the assembly = הָעֵדָה קְרִאֵי ; מ עלי ׳קרא Lam 1:15 called a festal meeting against me ; מ ׳בקרב Psa 74:4 in the midst of thine assembly ; מוֺעֵד הַר Isa 14:13 mount of meeting or assembly (of the gods; the mountain of the gods in the extreme north, the oriental Olympus, Persian Alborg , Hindu Meru , Babylon. Aralli , compare Len Origines ii, ch. ix ). 3 appointed place: a. the temple, || שׂכּוֺ Lam 2:6 , ממ ׳נוּגֵי afflicted (and driven) from the place of assembly Zeph 3:18 (compare Br MP 225 ). b. synagogues, בָּאָרֶץ כָּלמֿוֺעֲדֵיאֵֿל all the appointed places of El in the land Psa 74:8 = וַעַד בֵּית Sota 9:15 . 4 appointed sign, signal , Judg 20:38 . 5 מוֺעֵד אֹהֶל tent of meeting (of God with his people: see יָעַד Niph`al 1 ); the sacred tent of the Exodus (see אֹהֶל 3 ) Exod 33:7 (twice in verse); Num 12:4 ; Deut 31:14 (twice in verse) (E), Num 11:16 (J); often in P, as Exod 27:21 ; 29:4 ; Lev 1:1 , 3 ; Josh 18:1 ; 19:51 , etc. (131 t.)&gt;; elsewhere only 1Sam 2:22 b (omitted by ᵐ5 ), 1Kin 8:4 2Chr 5:5 ; 1Chr 6:17 ; 9:21 ; 23:32 ; 2Chr 1:3 , 6 , 13 .","rootNote":"or מֹעֵד ; or (feminine) מוֹעָדָה ; (2 Chronicles 8:13), from 3259 ;","sources":["MorphHB occurrences","Strong Hebrew Dictionary","Brown-Driver-Briggs"]},"firstMention":"1Chr 6 17","keyReferences":["1Chr 6 17","1Chr 9 21","1Chr 23 31","1Chr 23 32","1Kgs 8 4","1Sam 2 22","1Sam 9 24","1Sam 13 8"],"related":{"people":[],"places":[],"concepts":[],"events":[]},"occurrenceCount":223,"oc